"""
    BRMDescriptionTexts

Every text a model description writes itself: its prose sentences, the
meanings of the notation it introduces, the words inside its LaTeX, its
coverage-gap messages and the Markdown scaffold of
[`brm_description_markdown`](@ref). Build one with [`description_texts`](@ref)
and pass it as `texts=` to [`brm_description`](@ref); the description keeps it
and its Markdown follows it. Labels, units, symbols and hook prose are supplied
by the caller and are never translated.

A word in braces is a placeholder the description fills in, such as `{owner}`
or `{n_groups}`. Braces directly after a letter, `\\`, `_` or `^` are LaTeX,
not placeholders, so `\\textit{x}` and `a_{k}` stay literal. The texts named
`math_*` are LaTeX inserted into an equation.
"""
struct BRMDescriptionTexts
    locale::Symbol
    texts::NamedTuple
end

